00:38:06.840 --> 00:38:09.840
And this was alluding to what was to come the next day,

00:38:09.840 --> 00:38:11.840
which was his crucifixion.

00:38:11.840 --> 00:38:13.840
And he broke the bread and he said,

00:38:13.840 --> 00:38:17.840
this is my body,

00:38:17.840 --> 00:38:20.840
broken for you.

00:38:20.840 --> 00:38:23.840
If you'd like to go ahead, you can take your bread.

00:38:35.840 --> 00:38:40.840
And then Jesus held up a cup of wine.

00:38:41.840 --> 00:38:42.840
With his disciples.

00:38:42.840 --> 00:38:45.840
And he said, and this,

00:38:45.840 --> 00:38:48.840
this is my blood.

00:38:48.840 --> 00:38:49.840
Whenever you eat this bread,

00:38:49.840 --> 00:38:51.840
whenever you drink this cup,

00:38:51.840 --> 00:38:53.840
remember me.

00:38:53.840 --> 00:38:56.840
You can go ahead and take your wine.

00:39:00.840 --> 00:39:02.840
And so for 2000 years,

00:39:02.840 --> 00:39:06.840
Christians have participated in this,

00:39:06.840 --> 00:39:07.840
we call it a sacrament.

00:39:07.840 --> 00:39:08.840
It's this,

00:39:08.840 --> 00:39:12.840
these very simple elements

00:39:12.840 --> 00:39:14.840
that through God's presence

00:39:14.840 --> 00:39:20.840
become a sign of God's closeness to us.

00:39:22.840 --> 00:39:25.840
And so as you take them

00:39:25.840 --> 00:39:27.840
and as you reflect on these elements,

00:39:27.840 --> 00:39:29.840
I pray that you just remember

00:39:29.840 --> 00:39:32.840
that it's God drawing close to you.

00:39:33.840 --> 00:39:34.840
